        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Incline walking turns an easy walk into real cardio without the
            impact of running.</strong> At 3 mph, a 10% grade roughly doubles the estimated energy
            cost of the flat walk, raises heart rate substantially, and works the glutes,
            hamstrings and calves harder — but it builds little muscle for trained people and
            does not burn fat from anywhere in particular.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start at a modest grade, let go of the rails, stand tall, and build the incline over
            weeks to protect the calves and Achilles. For the trade-offs against running, see our
